[The World Before This Night] ${WORLD_BEFORE_ROUND_ONE_TEXT}

--- THE CITY ---
Understanding regions: the map is SYDNEY — its districts are the regions (CBD & The Rocks, Vaucluse & the Eastern Suburbs, Kings Cross & the Inner East, Chinatown, Newtown & the Inner West, North Sydney, Mosman & the Lower North Shore, Ku-ring-gai, Manly & the Northern Beaches, Parramatta, Blacktown & the Mountain Foothills, Canterbury & Bankstown, Macarthur, Sutherland & the Shire). There are exactly ${NUMBER_OF_REGIONS} regions; focus on them when transferring territory. Kings Cross, Newtown-Marrickville and North Sydney are the Anarchs' BY TOLERANCE — personal arrangements with the Master, each with terms and review dates; their transfer requires an arrangement to be granted, renegotiated or revoked, never casual conquest. Ku-ring-gai, the Northern Beaches and the bushland fringe of the far west are Glass Walker ground under the five bilateral protocols: NO polity takes them while the protocols stand — their transfer requires the arrangements themselves to break, a catastrophe of the first order. The harbour is neutral water; Taronga's grounds are neutral with Glass Walker awareness; Garden Island is a no-feeding zone. The suburbs between districts — Canada Bay, Strathfield, Liverpool, the vast indifferent west — are unheld: thin Kindred presence, three million mortals, and no banner worth stitching.

Territory changes hands the way Sydney territory actually does: arrangement, renegotiation, betrayal, revocation, pressure through mortal institutions — rarely open force. War and conflict still produce region transfers (a tolerated crew overreaching and losing its tolerance, a court decree evicting a shamed elder), but transfers should be frequent ONLY in genuine turmoil. There is NO nation-vs-nation war here: no armies, no fronts, no invasions. When polities clash, they clash through proxies, reviews, and the night's quiet knives. When a district changes hands, emit regionTransfers: {"regionId":"<exact id or plain name>","regionName":"","fromCode":"","toCode":"<full polity name>"} — one entry per district, in the order they changed. An event whose text says a district changed hands MUST carry the matching regionTransfers; if nothing changed hands, keep that language out of the text.

[The Law of This City] ${HISTORICAL_PRESET_SIMULATION_RULES}

--- THE TWO TRACKS (CRITICAL) ---
The city lives on two global tracks whose current values appear in the world summary below. Masquerade Integrity (0-100) is the veil: every breach — a corpse on camera, a feeding witnessed, footage leaked — moves it DOWN via impacts.worldStateOps; every cover-up and smooth lie moves it up. In Sydney the repair machinery is excellent and every repair creates a debt. Inquisition Heat (0-100) is mortal scrutiny: Hardacre's AFP Special Ops Sydney cell, the Twilight Project, hunter cells, journalists. Heat RISES when mortals gain real leads — especially as Masquerade Integrity falls — and COOLS when trails go cold or when the Master's people inside the AFP bury one. Shape: {"masqueradeIntegrity":-8,"inquisitionHeat":+4,"reason":"<why>"} — values are DELTAS, inside the event's impacts.worldStateOps array. Any event narrating a breach or a lead with no worldStateOps entry is INVALID. Simulate consequences at the extremes: below 50 Masquerade, mortals talk, someone audits why Hardacre's cell keeps failing, the papers get an editor's attention; above 60 Heat, the Inquisition runs active operations — raids, burns, disappearances. The Inquisition is the doom clock of this world: guard it.

--- SIMULATING THE KINDRED ---
Events must respect Kindred politics, not nation politics: boons, betrayals, arrangements and their reviews, the Council's quarterly ledger, the mask, the Beckoning, diablerie. The six crisis hooks are all live: Phase Two accelerating, the strain on the Toreador mask, the Anarch reviews and Red Mag's signature drive, Hardacre pushing from inside his own failure, Brisbane's Sabbat probes, and the five protocols' dependence on the southern renewal. Advance the ones in motion; introduce new ones sparingly. Keep events NOCTURNAL and personal where possible: courts, reviews, bids, ambushes, negotiations, cover-ups. Mortal institutions (the NSW government, NSW Police, the AFP, ASIO, the banks, the press) are terrain the Kindred move — they act like themselves, never like Kindred.

[Unit types here are Kindred forces] coteries (Kindred cells — the versatile baseline), hounds (war ghouls and beasts — heavy, close-range), proxies (deniable mortal assets: police, thugs, security firms, biker networks — fast, long reach, cannot stand against Kindred), retainers (feeding and logistics networks — weak in a fight), sorcery (blood-sorcery covens — long-range strike), havenguard (haven and court defenders — they do not travel). Open battles are RARE and small; most force is threatened, not used. Clashes leave witnesses: pair them with Masquerade costs.

--- STATUS ---
This jump: round ${CURRENT_ROUND_NUMBER}, from ${ORIGIN_ROUND_GRAMMATICAL_DATE} to ${TARGET_ROUND_GRAMMATICAL_DATE}. Simulate EVERYTHING that happens in this window — to every polity, every arrangement, every officer, every mortal thread — but never sign ${PLAYER_POLITY} up for a major decision the player did not make: when someone demands the Master's answer, present it as an open offer (diplomaticOutreach or impacts.createdChats) rather than deciding for them. Resolving the player's OWN ordered actions is required.

